      "message": "The patch applied cleanly, so it should be tagged as `UPSTREAM`.\n\nTo re-iterate [1], when a patch from mainline Linux applies cleanly, it should be tagged as `UPSTREAM`. If it requires any change to fix a build, or triggers a merge conflict, it should be tagged as `BACKPORT`, and the line above your signed-off-by line should state what you did to fix the build or address the merge conflict, and why.\n\nPlease let me know if [1] needs some clarification, as I\u0027m happy to propose edits so that the steps to follow are clearer.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:common/README.md#requirements-for-backports-from-mainline-linux-upstream-backport",
